<!--
  Quick Settings tile brand mark (issue #268).
  Derived from ic_launcher_monochrome.xml's isometric "black box" silhouette,
  re-fit to the 24dp QS tile viewport (the launcher drawable is authored on a
  108dp adaptive-icon canvas with its own safe-zone inset and cannot be
  pointed at directly for a tile).

  Simplified to the two dominant, highest-area subpaths of the source mark:
  the outer isometric hexagon silhouette and its primary top-face facet
  split (the two largest contours by bounding-box area in the source path,
  2474px^2 and 736px^2 respectively). The remaining seven subpaths in the
  source — the memory-cylinder rivet detail, the connector-pin facets, and
  hairline seam strokes (19px^2-279px^2 each) — are dropped: at a 24dp
  render size those already sub-pixel details would smear into noise rather
  than read as recognizable geometry, whereas the outer hexagon plus the
  top-face split still reads clearly as a 3D box silhouette.

  Single fill, no background layer, tintable via android:fillColor overrides
  (kept as white here per the QS tile contract: the system tints this icon,
  so no brand color is hardcoded).
-->
